<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Woodside WPL takes stake in offshore permit.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Woodside WPL takes stake in offshore permit.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Woodside Petroleum Ltd said on Monday it has reached an agreement with Cultus Timor Sea Ltd to acquire an 80-percent interest in the the offshore exploration permit Ashmore Cartier/P4 in Australia's Northern Territory.</p>
<p>The permit covers an area near the Australia-Indonesia Zone of Cooperation.</p>
<p>Woodside said it intends to farm out a portion of its interest to a third party.  </p>
<p>Over the next three years Woodside will carry Cultus for the costs associated with exploration work, which includes seismic acquisition of 1,100 line km of seismic data and the drilling of one exploration well, Cultus said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
